.alert.alert-light.border.mb-0
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Establish a shared baseline of ability milestones once. You and the other participant each rate privately per ability, then talk when both have rated that ability, then recognize and certify. After that, milestones move only when demonstrated. No full re-calibration.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render 'shared/maap/definition'

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-0
    %li
      %strong Expand for Ability details.
      Collapsed by default under each Ability: why it is on this page, the Ability description, all milestone definitions, recent OGOs where this person was rated on the Ability, and links to the teammate + Ability page and filtered OGOs.
    %li
      %strong Select to save.
      Choosing Milestone 0-5 saves immediately. First answer and any later change are both timestamped (cannot clear back to unanswered).
    %li
      %strong Ready to recognize and certify per ability.
      When both of you have rated an ability (Milestone 0-5), that ability shows both proposals so you can talk, then recognize and certify on this page (same certify meaning and optional comments as Award Milestone).
    %li
      %strong Audit trail.
      Under the status pills you will see each person’s first selection and last change (value and time), so changing after seeing the other answer is visible.
    %li
      %strong Milestone 0 is a real answer.
      It means no Milestone earned yet for that ability. Leaving a rating blank is “not answered.”
    %li
      Prefer this ritual over bulk award when establishing a baseline. Bulk award remains for edge cases only.
